I"T<p>We had a situation where a new pdb(19.6.0.0) was created to receive a import from another database(11.2.0.1) that had Oracle Spatial installed and the target database didn’t.
Weirdly executing a full import to the pdb “installed” a flawed version of the Spatial feature in the CDB. It appeared in the dba_registry and cdb_registry views, but it was invalid.</p>

<p><a href="/assets/2020-09-24-import-full-to-pdb-oracle-spatial-problems_spatial_invalid.jpeg"><img src="/assets/2020-09-24-import-full-to-pdb-oracle-spatial-problems_spatial_invalid.jpeg" alt="" /></a></p>

<p>After a database restart the PDBs opened in restricted session mode, even PDB$SEED.</p>

<p><a href="/assets/2020-09-24-import-full-to-pdb-oracle-spatial-problems_pdb_restricted_yes.jpeg"><img src="/assets/2020-09-24-import-full-to-pdb-oracle-spatial-problems_pdb_restricted_yes.jpeg" alt="" /></a></p>

